{
 "formato": "sktch",
 "versao": 1,
 "gerado": "demo do CircuitSketch",
 "descricao": [
  "MUSIC PLAYER (DAP): a player in the style of the Surfans F20, on an",
  "ESP32-S3.",
  "",
  "The PlayerDAP library, in C, runs in native mode: it plays MP3, FLAC, WAV,",
  "AIFF, OGG Vorbis, Opus, ALAC, WavPack and DSD, reads the tags and sorts by",
  "artist, album, genre, album artist, year, composer and folder. It makes",
  "playlists, keeps favorites, has a five-band equalizer and five play modes",
  "(all, repeat once, repeat always, shuffle, shuffle the list).",
  "",
  "BEFORE RUNNING: the music does not come with it. Double-click the card and",
  "use \"Use a folder from the computer...\" to choose your music folder",
  "(nothing is copied). The flash drive also takes a folder; click it to",
  "remove it and plug it back with the player on.",
  "",
  "Press F5 and click the circuit. The arrows go up and down (the wheel),",
  "Enter is OK (the wheel click), Backspace goes back (held: repeat), M is",
  "MODE (held: favorite), Space pauses, Page Up and Page Down change the",
  "volume. F2 is the power switch and F3 removes and plugs in the flash",
  "drive. Change the battery voltage to watch the charge change (below 3.3 V",
  "the player turns off).",
  "",
  "On the real board: ESP32-S3 N8R8 or N16R8, \"OPI PSRAM\", a partition with",
  "3 MB of app, and the library from bibliotecas/PlayerDAP in the Arduino",
  "IDE's libraries folder. The flash drive needs Espressif's usb_host_msc",
  "component and 5 V on VBUS; the battery powers the board through a charger",
  "with a regulator."
 ],
 "codigo": [
  "// Music player (DAP) with the ESP32-S3: microSD card and USB flash drive,",
  "// portrait ILI9341 screen, click wheel (KY-040), five buttons, power",
  "// switch, battery measured by the ADC and I2S sound on the MAX98357A.",
  "//",
  "// Plays MP3, FLAC, WAV, AIFF, OGG Vorbis, Opus, ALAC (M4A), WavPack and DSD",
  "// (DSF and DFF); AAC, WMA and APE show up in the list, but do not play. It",
  "// reads the tags and sorts the songs by artist, album, genre, album",
  "// artist, year, composer and folder; makes playlists (.m3u8 in the card's",
  "// /Playlists folder) and keeps the favorites.",
  "//",
  "// The wheel moves through the lists, and its click is OK. BACK goes back",
  "// one screen (held: changes the repeat). MODE opens favorite, equalizer and",
  "// play mode (held: favorites the song playing). PAUSE plays and pauses",
  "// (held: stops). On the \"Now playing\" screen, the wheel changes song; a",
  "// click on it makes the wheel seek back and forth within the song.",
  "#include <player_dap.h>",
  "#include \"esp_sleep.h\"",
  "",
  "const int POWER = 1;      // power switch: LOW is on (10k to 3V3)",
  "const int BATTERY = 2;    // the middle of the battery's 100k + 100k divider",
  "",
  "void setup() {",
  "  Serial.begin(115200);",
  "  pinMode(POWER, INPUT_PULLUP);",
  "  if (digitalRead(POWER) == HIGH) sleepUntil(0);   // woke up with the switch off",
  "",
  "  int mv = battery();",
  "  if (empty(mv)) {",
  "    Serial.println(\"Battery empty: charge it, then switch off and on.\");",
  "    sleepUntil(1);",
  "  }",
  "",
  "  dap_barramento(11, 13, 12);       // MOSI, MISO and SCK: the screen and the card",
  "  dap_tela(10, 9, 8, 7);            // CS, DC, RST and the screen backlight",
  "  dap_cartao(14);                   // microSD CS",
  "  dap_usb(1);                       // the flash drive on the S3's USB (GPIO 19 and 20)",
  "  dap_som(40, 41, 42, 96000);       // BCLK, LRC, DIN and the DAC's highest rate",
  "  dap_botoes(17, 18, 21, 38, 39);   // volume +, volume -, back, mode, pause",
  "  dap_roda(4, 5, 6);                // CLK, DT and the wheel click",
  "  dap_bateria(mv);",
  "  dap_iniciar();",
  "}",
  "",
  "void loop() {",
  "  int mv = battery();",
  "  dap_bateria(mv);",
  "  if (digitalRead(POWER) == HIGH) {",
  "    dap_desligar();                 // saves where it stopped and turns off the screen",
  "    sleepUntil(0);",
  "  }",
  "  if (empty(mv)) {",
  "    Serial.println(\"Battery empty.\");",
  "    dap_desligar();",
  "    sleepUntil(1);",
  "  }",
  "  delay(250);",
  "}",
  "",
  "// The divider cuts the battery voltage in half (4.2 V becomes 2.1 V).",
  "int battery() {",
  "  return analogReadMilliVolts(BATTERY) * 2;",
  "}",
  "",
  "// Below 3.3 V the lithium cell gets damaged. With no battery connected the",
  "// reading is zero, and then the USB is what powers the board.",
  "bool empty(int mv) {",
  "  return mv > 1000 && mv < 3300;",
  "}",
  "",
  "// Sleeps until the switch goes to the requested level: 0 to turn on, or 1",
  "// (empty battery) to only turn back on after switching off.",
  "void sleepUntil(int level) {",
  "  Serial.println(level == 0 ? \"Off: the board sleeps until the switch turns on again.\"",
  "                            : \"The board sleeps until the switch turns off.\");",
  "  esp_sleep_enable_ext0_wakeup(GPIO_NUM_1, level);",
  "  esp_deep_sleep_start();",
  "}"
 ],
 "circuito": {
  "Pecas": [
   {
    "Id": "placa",
    "Tipo": "esp32-s3-devkit",
    "X": 520,
    "Y": 160,
    "Usb": true
   },
   {
    "Id": "tela",
    "Tipo": "ili9341",
    "X": 40,
    "Y": 110,
    "Nome": "display 240x320 (ILI9341)"
   },
   {
    "Id": "cartao",
    "Tipo": "microsd-card",
    "X": 380,
    "Y": 420,
    "Nome": "microSD card",
    "Arquivos": {
     "README.TXT": "MUSIC PLAYER: where the music lives\n\nThis card has no music yet. Double-click it and use \"Use a folder from\nthe computer...\" to choose your music folder: everything in it, with the\nsubfolders, shows up on the card. Nothing is copied, and the folder never\nchanges: what the player saves (playlists, favorites, where it stopped)\nstays on the project's card.\n\nThe flash drive also takes a folder. Click the flash drive to remove it\nand plug it back with the player on: the library is read again.\n\nPlays MP3, FLAC, WAV, AIFF, OGG Vorbis, Opus, ALAC (.m4a), WavPack, DSF and\nDFF. The playlists are the .m3u and .m3u8 files in the /Playlists folder\n(the ones from the computer work).\n"
    }
   },
